  "audio": "023.now-we-arrive.mp3",
  "paragraph": 23,
  "text": "Now we arrive at Pillar Four, arguably the single highest-leverage multiplier in any harness: turning probabilistic outputs into trustworthy engineering. An open-loop agent writes code and hopes it compiles. A closed-loop harness wires verification directly into deterministic checks: unit tests, typecheckers, browser assertions, and instant IDE language-server and linter feedback like Cursor and Windsurf provide. Top harnesses even add an explicit self-check pass where the agent audits its own git diff against requirements before finishing. Ground-truth feedback turns a probabilistic guesser into a reliable self-correcting engineer.",
